Data artifacts

Everything else under projects/: the vendored incident corpora, the derived
labels and gold sets, the calibration outputs, posteriors, and blended
rankings, the baselines and taxonomies, and the provenance and
pre-registration manifests that describe them.

Derived from publicly available incident datasets and distributed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC-BY-4.0).
See https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ for details.

Note that this is CC-BY-4.0, not the CC BY-SA 4.0 that covers the published
content. The data carries no ShareAlike obligation, so a downstream analysis
may reuse the corpus and labels under terms of its own choosing.

Incident records in these artifacts carry internal identifiers of the form
INC-04490 rather than upstream CVE, GHSA, OSV, or AIAAIC keys. The source
databases retain their own terms and remain the authority for the underlying
incident descriptions. What this repository redistributes is derived labels
and snapshots.

